## '...' in an argument list

fun g(x y) { return x }

fun f(a ...) { g(... a) } ##ERROR: syntax error - '...' allowed only as the last argument

---

## the same when it is buried among other arguments

fun g(x y z) { return x }

fun f(a ...) { g(a ... a) } ##ERROR: syntax error - '...' allowed only as the last argument

---

## twice in one call - the first one is not last, so it is caught the same way

fun g(x y) { return x }

fun f(...) { g(... ...) } ##ERROR: syntax error - '...' allowed only as the last argument

---

## relaying from a function that collects nothing
##
## Refusing this beats relaying an empty pack silently: the '...' says the
## author believed there was something to pass on.

fun g(x) { return x }

fun f(a) { g(a ...) } ##ERROR: syntax error - '...' not usable in a function that has no '...' parameter

---

## and outside any function at all

fun g(x) { return x }

g(1 ...) ##ERROR: syntax error - '...' not usable in a function that has no '...' parameter

---

## a message send argument list is checked the same way

class K { fun[#c] m(a b) { return a } }

fun f(...) { return K:m(... 1) } ##ERROR: syntax error - '...' allowed only as the last argument
